<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uppsala University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1477</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a> University was founded in 1477 by Archbishop Jakob Ulvsson with a papal bull of Sixtus IV and the support of the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder">Sten Sture the Elder</a>, making it the oldest university in the Nordic countries. It declined after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> but was refounded in the 1590s and became the centre of Swedish learning, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-linnaeus">Carl Linnaeus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anders-celsius">Anders Celsius</a> taught.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uppsala-university.jpg" alt="Uppsala University" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ScanianDragon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uppsala_University_2023.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
